findings.body:
The `tauri` crate moves to 2.8.3 here, but the metadata file the CLI embeds wasn't synced. `cli.js.version` was bumped; `tauri` was not.

::diff{file="crates/tauri-cli/metadata-v2.json" lines="1-9"}

The `tauri` package in `.changes/config.json` has a `postversion` hook that runs `sync-cli-metadata.js tauri patch`. Every earlier release, such as #14041 (`2.8.1 → 2.8.2`), bumped this field together with the crate version. So either the hook didn't run for `tauri`, or its output was dropped.

::callout{type="warning"}
`metadata-v2.json` is compiled into the CLI with `include_str!`. `crates/tauri-cli/src/init.rs:220` and `src/plugin/init.rs:118-119` write `metadata.tauri` into the generated Cargo.toml. As a result, the 2.8.1 CLI will scaffold new projects with `tauri = "2.8.2"`, which is the version without the WebView2 FixedRuntime fix this release ships. A fresh resolve still picks 2.8.3 because of semver, but the pinned minimum is wrong and the release metadata disagrees with itself.


::suggestion{file="crates/tauri-cli/metadata-v2.json" lines="6-6"}
  "tauri": "2.8.3",

The new `tauri-cli` 2.8.1 changelog entry says:

::diff{file="crates/tauri-cli/CHANGELOG.md" lines="3-8"}

But the dependency requirement in `crates/tauri-cli/Cargo.toml` wasn't touched:

::code{file="crates/tauri-cli/Cargo.toml" lines="50-50"}

The previous release (#13887) bumped this line together with the bundler (`2.5.2 → 2.6.0`), so covector's dependency rewrite was skipped here. Cargo.lock resolves to 2.6.1 through the path dependency, so local and `--locked` builds are fine. However, the published `tauri-cli` 2.8.1 would declare that it works with `tauri-bundler` 2.6.0. That is the version with the 32-bit Windows binary-patching bug this release exists to fix. Unlocked installs or downstream resolution could pick 2.6.0, which contradicts the changelog.

::suggestion{file="crates/tauri-cli/Cargo.toml" lines="50-50"}
tauri-bundler = { version = "2.6.1", default-features = false, path = "../tauri-bundler" }
